<p>Israeli Finance Minister Bezalel Smotrich said Israel should extend its border with Lebanon to the Litani River, openly calling for the annexation of part of southern Lebanon as Israeli attacks in the area intensified. Israel says its operations in southern Lebanon target Hezbollah after the group fired missiles into Israel on March 2. The proposal matters because it shows some Israeli officials are openly discussing redrawing the frontier, not just pushing Hezbollah back from it.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/wRs_aG1_4qGSDChEqmjZK6OD8eLx4BjfyLIgWT-lDRFy7RyTIAs-U6DEf0kNukL_H-0l93smDUYu5I7ohWt6Jst1Jqno4LCqBir1t3bO8GQw' alt='Israeli soldiers stand next to tanks near the Israeli side of the border with Lebanon, amid escalation between Hezbollah and Israel, in northern Israel on March 23, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Escalation signal: Dawn described Smotrich’s remarks as the clearest call yet by a senior Israeli official to seize Lebanese territory.</li><li>Ground-war fears: France 24 reported that a strike on a key bridge in Lebanon deepened fears that the campaign could expand into a ground invasion.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Bezalel Smotrich: In radio comments, he said the Lebanon campaign should end with &quot;a different reality entirely,&quot; linking a decision on Hezbollah with a change in Israel’s borders. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1984622/israeli-minister-calls-for-annexation-of-southern-lebanon-extension-of-border'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Israeli military position: Israel has framed its operations in southern Lebanon as action against Hezbollah and describes the area south of the Litani as a Hezbollah stronghold. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1984622/israeli-minister-calls-for-annexation-of-southern-lebanon-extension-of-border'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Lebanese reaction: Dawn said the annexation talk is especially sensitive in Lebanon because memories of Israel’s 1982 invasion and subsequent occupation remain vivid. 